les, and I didn't commit.\n\nWhat changed, following SPEC.md:\n\n- **`ForeignKey`** is now a dataclass with `columns`, `other_columns`, `is_compound`, `on_delete` and `on_update`. It is no longer a tuple, so unpacking or indexing raises `TypeError`.\n- **Reading keys:** `Table.foreign_keys` groups `PRAGMA foreign_key_list` rows by `id`, so compound keys come back as one key, with their actions. A `REFERENCES other` with no columns resolves to the other table's primary key.\n- **Creating and altering:** compound keys are emitted as table-level `FOREIGN KEY (...) REFERENCES ...` lines. `resolve_foreign_keys`, `add_foreign_keys`, `add_foreign_key` and `transform` accept, keep, rename and drop compound keys. `index_foreign_keys` creates one composite index per compound key.\n\nTwo calls the spec didn't spell out:\n- `add_foreign_keys` raises `ValueError` when a 4-tuple has different numbers of columns on each side. The spec only covered that case for the other entry points.\n- The `ForeignKey` equality and sort order follow the spec's `compare=False` on `column`/`other_column`, so mixed compound and single keys sort without `None`/`str` errors.\n\nThe test run now also shows 23 Click `isolated_filesystem` DeprecationWarnings from `tests/test_cli.py`. They come from existing tests, not from this change; my first run didn't show them, so they likely depend on the installed Click version.", "ttft_ms": 1848, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 216171, "uuid": "c02f926c-f91c-480c-8de9-74c186506d0e", "ttft_stream_ms": 1616, "time_to_request_ms": 418, "first_content_frame_ms": 1616, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
